# Dependencies
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# Environment
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
# apps/mobile/.env is a committed exception: EAS Build's Gradle-invoked
# Metro bundling step reads EXPO_PUBLIC_* values from an actual .env
# file on disk, not from EAS's injected process env (confirmed directly
# via a build that had the EAS env vars set but produced a bundle with
# zero occurrences of the Supabase URL - the app crashed on launch
# because of it). The two values in that file are the same
# publishable/anon-safe class already shipped inside the compiled
# bundle either way - committing them is not a new exposure.
!apps/mobile/.env

